  "tips": {
    "ask": [
      "The question word sits where the answer goes: 你叫什么名字？ is literally 'You are called what name?'",
      "Tones matter. The mark over the pinyin shows the tone: mā high and flat, má rising, mǎ dipping, mà falling.",
      "For yes, people often say 对 duì (right) or repeat the verb. 不 bù is no / not."
    ],
    "name": [
      "To turn any sentence into a yes/no question, add 吗 ma at the end: 这是狗吗？",
      "You can't say 一狗 (one dog). You need a measure word: 一只狗, 一本书, 一辆车. 个 gè works for lots of things.",
      "There's no word for 'the', and verbs never change. Less to learn!"
    ],
    "where": [
      "Word order: thing + 在 zài + place + position. 猫在桌子上 = cat at table on-top.",
      "The position word (上, 里, 下面, 旁边) comes after the place, not before."
    ],
    "want": [
      "要 yào = want (a thing). 想 xiǎng = would like to (do something). 我要水. 我想睡觉.",
      "The verb is the same for everyone: 我要, 你要, 他要."
    ],
    "like": [
      "Don't have is 没有 méiyǒu, never 不有.",
      "喜欢 + an action: 我喜欢游泳 = I like swimming.",
      "Brothers and sisters are older or younger: 弟弟 little brother, 姐姐 big sister."
    ],
    "describe": [
      "Use 很 hěn to join a thing and a describing word: 车很大 (car very big). Don't use 是 here.",
      "Describing a noun: colour + 的 + noun: 红色的车 (red car)."
    ],
    "do": [
      "Time words go before the verb: 我每天游泳 (I every day swim).",
      "去 qù + place. No word for 'to' needed: 我去学校."
    ],
    "people": [
      "Verbs never change! 我吃, 他吃, 我们吃.",
      "他 (he) and 她 (she) sound exactly the same: tā. Only the writing is different."
    ],
    "time": [
      "There are no tenses. Add a time word (昨天 yesterday, 明天 tomorrow) and the meaning changes.",
      "Add 了 le at the end when something is finished: 昨天我游泳了.",
      "要 yào before an action means 'going to': 明天我要游泳."
    ],
    "join": [
      "因为 yīnwèi = because, 但是 dànshì = but.",
      "和 hé = and, but only between two nouns (a dog and a cat), not between two sentences."
    ]
  }
}
